{"hash":"25327f9c64110ddd","voice":"en-IN-NeerjaExpressiveNeural","rate":"+4%","dur":81.619,"said":"Sit a while here in the Sabha Mandap, under the golden dome, close to the sanctum. Five times a day aarti is offered to Baba Vishwanath, and the temple trust keeps the hours: the Mangala Aarti before dawn, between three and four; the midday Bhog Aarti; the Saptarishi Aarti in the evening, from seven; the Shringar and Bhog Aarti at nine. And last of all, at half past ten at night, the Shayan Aarti. Shayan means sleep. This is the aarti that puts the Lord to rest, offered with the care one would give a beloved elder at the end of the day: a bed of flowers is made ready, sandalwood paste is offered, and the lamps are waved one last time as the hymns grow soft. At eleven the doors close. For a few short hours the city that never sleeps lets its Lord sleep, until the bells of the Mangala Aarti wake him again before dawn. Devotees call it the gentlest darshan of the day, and say it brings peace of mind and a restful night to those who stand before him then. The aarti you hear in the sanctum is sung for this hour: Jai Hari Hara. Har Har Mahadev.\n\nDid you know? The trust's timings: Shringar and Bhog Aarti at 9 PM, Shayan Aarti at 10:30 PM; the temple closes at 11.","segments":[{"key":"text","start":0,"end":1054},{"key":"didYouKnow","start":1070,"end":1174}],"words":[[0.098,0.264,0,3],[0.374,0.12,4,5],[0.507,0.264,6,11],[0.783,0.337,12,16],[1.132,0.084,17,19],[1.228,0.084,20,23],[1.324,0.349,24,29],[1.685,0.505,30,36],[2.406,0.216,38,43],[2.634,0.096,44,47],[2.742,0.421,48,54],[3.175,0.397,55,59],[3.836,0.312,61,66],[4.161,0.108,67,69],[4.281,0.096,70,73],[4.389,0.613,74,81],[5.901,0.397,83,87],[6.31,0.373,88,93],[6.695,0.084,94,95],[6.791,0.288,96,99],[7.091,0.457,100,105],[7.56,0.144,106,108],[7.716,0.397,109,116],[8.125,0.108,117,119],[8.245,0.397,120,124],[8.654,0.685,125,135],[9.519,0.18,137,140],[9.712,0.084,141,144],[9.808,0.433,145,151],[10.252,0.349,152,157],[10.613